<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/red-house-snow.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/red-house-snow-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/red-house-snow.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><a href="/towns-we-cover/">Towns we cover</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Brunswick</span></nav><p class="kicker">Midcoast · Cumberland County</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Brunswick, Maine</h1><p class="lede">Brunswick’s historic Maine Street homes, wooded rural roads and Casco Bay shorefront each bring their own claim problems. We review carrier estimates for homes and businesses and serve as appraiser when the amount is disputed.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-coral" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg><span>Call (844) 537-1427</span></a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/reach-us/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="spec"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Cumberland County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Midcoast</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><div class="snap"><h2>Brunswick at a glance</h2><dl>
<div><dt>County</dt><dd>Cumberland County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Midcoast</dd></div>
<div class="wide"><dt>Neighborhoods and villages</dt><dd><ul class="chips"><li>Downtown Maine Street</li><li>Bowdoin College area</li><li>Mere Point</li><li>Pennellville</li><li>Cook’s Corner</li><li>Brunswick Landing</li><li>Topsham</li></ul></dd></div>
<div class="wide"><dt>Housing mix</dt><dd>Federal and Greek Revival homes near Maine Street and the college, connected farmhouses and capes on the rural roads, shorefront homes on Mere Point and Maquoit Bay, and newer housing on the former naval air station at Brunswick Landing.</dd></div>
<div class="wide"><dt>Common claim risks</dt><dd><ul class="chips coral"><li>Fallen pines</li><li>Ice dams</li><li>Coastal wind</li><li>Puffback soot</li></ul></dd></div></dl>
<h3>Storms on record</h3><ol class="mini-storms"><li><b>Oct 2017</b><span><strong>October windstorm.</strong> Record statewide outages; tall pines snapped onto roofs and lines across the Midcoast.</span></li><li><b>Jan 2024</b><span><strong>Back-to-back coastal storms.</strong> Record tides damaged wharves and shore roads in neighboring Harpswell and around Casco Bay.</span></li><li><b>Jan 1998</b><span><strong>Ice Storm of 1998.</strong> Heavy ice brought down trees and power lines across southern and central Maine for days.</span></li></ol></div>
<h2>Old houses, tall trees</h2>
<p>Brunswick, at the northern edge of Cumberland County, is where many people say the Midcoast begins. Around the Bowdoin College campus and along Maine Street, the housing is old: Federal and Greek Revival homes with plaster walls, original trim and multi-pane windows. Out on the rural roads, connected farmhouses sit under tall white pines. Many of the Brunswick claims we hear about start with one of those trees.</p>
<p>When the October 2017 windstorm swept through, it caused record power outages statewide, and Midcoast towns were left with snapped pines across roofs, porches and ells. Tree claims look simple until you add crane time, removal limits, and the hidden framing damage that only shows once the trunk is gone. An insurance appraiser in Brunswick looks at all of it. Our <a href="/appraisal-work/fallen-tree-limb-appraisal/">fallen tree and limb appraisal</a> page explains how those claims break down.</p>
<h2>The connected farmhouse problem</h2>
<p>“Big house, little house, back house, barn.” Brunswick has plenty of these connected buildings, and they complicate claims. A roof collapse in the ell can damage the main house; snow sliding off one roof can tear gutters and trim off another. Carriers sometimes treat outbuildings and attached structures under different coverage parts, which affects limits. The policy decides that question. The estimate still needs to capture each building correctly.</p>
<h2>Shorefront and the bay</h2>
<p>Mere Point, Maquoit Bay and the shore roads toward Harpswell face Casco Bay. The January 2024 storms brought record tides, damaging wharves and shore roads in neighboring Harpswell. Surge and wave damage are flood and typically excluded under homeowners policies, but wind damage to roofs and siding is usually part of the property claim.</p>
<h2>Heat, oil and winter</h2>
<p>Many older Brunswick homes still heat with oil, and a burner puffback can coat every room in fine soot. The Ice Storm of January 1998 showed what long outages do: frozen pipes and water damage followed in homes that lost heat. Before cleanup, read our <a href="/owner-guides/oil-burner-puffback-documentation/">puffback documentation guide</a>.</p>
<h3>What we look for</h3>
<ul>
<li>Plaster, original trim and old windows on Maine Street homes priced as modern materials.</li>
<li>Framing and ell damage hidden under a fallen tree.</li>
<li>Cleaning scopes that skip closets, ducts and contents after puffback.</li>
<li>Newer Brunswick Landing homes where matching siding and roofing still matter.</li>
</ul>
<p>Brunswick Landing adds a newer layer to the town’s housing. Homes and commercial buildings on the former naval air station are recent construction, but newer does not mean simple: siding, roofing and window lines can be discontinued within a few years, and partial repairs raise the same matching questions as an old cape. Topsham, across the Androscoggin, shares much of the same mix of older village homes and newer subdivisions.</p>
<p>A Brunswick insurance appraiser resolves the amount of loss, not coverage. For coverage disputes or deadline questions, consult a Maine attorney.</p>

<h2>Appraisal work for Brunswick properties</h2>
<p>Every Maine Insurance Appraiser service is available in Brunswick and the surrounding towns, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/appraisal-work/homeowner-dispute-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/noreaster-hurricane-appraisal/">Nor’easter &amp; Hurricane Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/water-damage-loss-appraisal/">Water Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/ice-dam-snow-load-appraisal/">Ice Dam &amp; Snow Load Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/fallen-tree-limb-appraisal/">Fallen Tree Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/carrier-estimate-line-review/">Insurance Estimate Review</a></li></ul>
<h2>Brunswick questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>A pine fell on my Brunswick farmhouse ell. Is the whole connected building one claim?</summary><p>It often is, but policies can treat attached and detached structures differently. Your policy language decides coverage, and the estimate should capture damage to each part of the building.</p></details><details><summary>Does the carrier have to pay for crane time to remove a tree from my roof?</summary><p>Many policies cover reasonable debris and tree removal tied to covered damage, sometimes with limits. Read your policy, and make sure the estimate reflects the equipment actually needed.</p></details><details><summary>Can appraisal help with a puffback claim in an older Brunswick home?</summary><p>Yes, if the dispute is about the amount. Appraisers can look at whether cleaning, repainting and contents work were scoped for the whole home.</p></details></div>
